    {
      "id": "claim_cc9445126a7e4734949cbe0a557bf4f2",
      "statement": "Komodo derives a stack's Compose project name from the Komodo Stack name, overriding a compose file's `name:`, so renaming a live stack cannot be done by editing compose — it requires a down-old / up-new cutover that removes only the old containers and preserves the external volumes and networks, because a Docker volume's name is its identity and recreating it empty would lose the stored per-user data.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/proposals/volume-network-rename-migration.md#L7-L17",
