    {
      "id": "claim_c7928301a1c841268eb8ed05e99cc488",
      "statement": "The two production Mongo stores are deliberately asymmetric: mc-service-store-mongo is a single-member replica set whose keyfile implies --auth (so it needs the keyfile plus SCRAM users), while mcm-bff-store-mongo is standalone and needs SCRAM credentials only and never a keyfile, since a standalone mongod has no replica-set members to authenticate; only MONGO_MC_APP_PASSWORD, MONGO_MC_KEYFILE and MONGO_BFF_APP_PASSWORD are wired into running services, the two *_ROOT_PASSWORD values are setup-only, and under --auth the replica-set self-init healthcheck was replaced by a credential-less ping because rs.status()/rs.initiate() require authentication.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-data-tier-auth.md#L30-L38",
