    {
      "id": "claim_10c78403290747bea3c7f83ee3c8d376",
      "statement": "main's required status checks are read live from branch protection for the target's base branch rather than hand-maintained, with the committed list in scripts/ci-status.mjs as a reported fallback only — currently seven globs: guardrails*, app-ci / changes*, app-ci / affected*, app-ci / mc-service-checks*, app-ci / app-e2e*, infra-image-scan / infra-image-scan*, and the later app-ci / app-image-scan* (spec 084 US3). The fallback is used when the read fails or when no status-check rule covers the branch, and its use is always named in the verdict header rather than silently substituted, because the hand-maintained mirror once held five globs while main required six — feature 035 had added infra-image-scan and nobody mirrored it — and ci-status printed VERDICT mergeable + exit 0 while the merge API answered 405, the over-reporting direction in which an automated status-and-merge wrapper attempts a merge that cannot succeed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/__tests__/ci-status.test.mjs#L839-L858",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be4690c608fb1de42a5b2ebb58c71dca7f0db43872e79655b85bc6ac22ab5466:"
        },
