        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3e172e81588547c3800cec425b67004a",
      "statement": "The committed fallback required-context list is constrained to be a SUBSET of what branch protection actually requires: a fallback glob that protection does not require would mark a check required that is not and block a mergeable PR, so lagging behind live protection is tolerable (the live fetch catches it) while over-claiming is not — asserted by a test that requires every fallback glob to appear in the live list, plus a belt-and-braces assertion that the fallback carries the very glob whose absence produced the 405. trigger-cd and dast are deliberately absent from it because branch protection does not require them, which is what keeps their failures advisory rather than blocking.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/__tests__/ci-status.test.mjs#L324-L330",
